# CAVEAT — read before assuming this is doing anything:
# The Dockerfile in this directory MUST be built with the repo root as
# the build context (pnpm workspace deps — see Dockerfile's own doc
# comment). Plain `docker build`/BuildKit look for the ignore file at
# <context-root>/.dockerignore (or <context-root>/<dockerfile-path>.dockerignore
# for BuildKit's per-Dockerfile convention) — NOT at
# apps/sbp-agent/.dockerignore when the context is the repo root. This
# file may therefore be silently ignored depending on how `flyctl deploy`
# resolves its context. See FLY_DEPLOY.md for how to verify, and copy
# this file to the repo root (or the BuildKit-specific name) if the build
# log shows node_modules/.env being sent to the build context.
#
# The Dockerfile's own explicit COPY list (not `COPY . .`) is the primary
# defence against shipping these paths — this file is a secondary
# safeguard, not the only one.

node_modules
dist
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
.env.example
test
*.test.ts
.git
.gitignore
*.md
railway.json
render.yaml
